+        code: "ffi_parameter_type",
+        message: "`" + parts[1] + "` of `" + parts[0] + "` lends a whole record to C as `void *`, and nothing says how many bytes C may reach through it: the count is another argument C reads, and this declaration ties none to the record",
+        span: found.must().span
+    )
+    d.notes @ d.notes.push(
+        "name the parameter that carries the count, `@" + parts[1] + ": <record> counted_by <count>`, and the call is held to the record's size before C runs"
+    )
